1 START

   Starts a batch queue, or the queue manager.

2 /QUEUE

   Starts a batch queue on this node, so that it runs its jobs, or lets
   a queue that STOP/QUEUE paused go on.  START/QUEUE takes
   INITIALIZE/QUEUE's attributes, and changes them as it starts the
   queue.  A queue already started is %JBC-E-STARTED.  It needs manage
   access to the queue (%JBC-E-NOPRIV).

   Format

     START/QUEUE queue-name

3 Parameter

 queue-name

   The queue to start.

3 Qualifiers
/QUEUE

   Selects START/QUEUE.

/BASE_PRIORITY

      /BASE_PRIORITY=n

   The base priority, 0 to 31, of the queue's jobs' processes.  The
   default is 4.

/CPUDEFAULT

      /[NO]CPUDEFAULT=hh:mm:ss

   The CPU time limit a job gets when it gives none.  INFINITE is no
   limit.

/CPUMAXIMUM

      /[NO]CPUMAXIMUM=hh:mm:ss

   The most CPU time a job may ask for.

/DESCRIPTION

      /[NO]DESCRIPTION="text"

   A line of text describing the queue, which SHOW QUEUE shows.

/JOB_LIMIT

      /JOB_LIMIT=n

   How many jobs the queue runs at once, 1 to 255.  The default is 1.

/OWNER_UIC

      /OWNER_UIC=uic

   The queue's owner, a UIC or an identifier.  The default is [SYSTEM].

/PROTECTION

      /PROTECTION=(category:access[,...])

   The queue's protection code.  A queue's kinds of access are R (read:
   see its jobs), S (submit), M (manage), and D (delete: change or
   delete one's own jobs).  The default is (S:M,O:D,G:R,W:S).  SET
   SECURITY/CLASS=QUEUE changes it too, and the queue's ACL.

/RETAIN

      /[NO]RETAIN[=option]

   Which ended jobs the queue keeps: ALL (the default option) or ERROR,
   those that didn't succeed.  /NORETAIN keeps none.

/WSDEFAULT

      /[NO]WSDEFAULT=n

   The queue's working-set default for its jobs, in pages.  govax keeps
   and shows the working-set values; a job's process has its account's.

/WSEXTENT

      /[NO]WSEXTENT=n

   The queue's working-set extent for its jobs, in pages.

/WSQUOTA

      /[NO]WSQUOTA=n

   The queue's working-set quota for its jobs, in pages.

3 Examples

   1.$ START/QUEUE SYS$BATCH

     Starts SYS$BATCH.

3 /MANAGER

   Starts the queue manager, which keeps the queues and runs their
   jobs.  The queue database is a host file (the configuration key
   vax.queue.file, by default ~/.govax/qman.json), which the first start
   makes.  The manager runs in one govax session at a time: another
   session may show the queues but not change them.  Once started, the
   manager starts again with each session until STOP/QUEUE/MANAGER.  It
   needs the OPER and SYSNAM privileges (%JBC-E-NOPRIV).

   Format

     START/QUEUE/MANAGER [directory]

4 Parameter

 directory

   VMS's directory for the database's files.  govax records it, and
   SHOW QUEUE/MANAGER/FULL shows it, but the database stays the host
   file.

4 Qualifiers
/MANAGER

   Selects START/QUEUE/MANAGER.
